{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Then the angels returned.</b> Meaning: they brought him back an answer and said to him <b>we came to your brother</b> — meaning, he shows a face of being your brother, but in truth he is Esau, inscribed with hatred. <b>and he is also coming toward you,</b> etc. — meaning, he is coming toward you in a manner of brotherhood, and four hundred men are with him for an evil design." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that <b>we came to your brother</b> [was said] with a showing of friendly countenances, and they also showed him countenances of wrath, on the side of the fact that in truth he is Esau without brotherhood. And this is along the lines of what they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah chapter 75), that they showed him camps of fire-riders, etc., to frighten him lest he not conduct himself with the quality of brotherhood. And the reason they did not establish the mission in a single manner is because his face showed brotherhood yet his heart was not so — therefore they made two modes of mission, whether for good, whether, etc.:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:29.636068207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}